<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Jstat (200)</h1>
<p><b>Work in progress: jstat isn't finished.</b>
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>jstat room|zone|memory|account|creators|count|world
jstat &lt;someone or something&gt; [data|contents|affects|descriptor|...]
</pre>
<p>The same as <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>, with the same arguments, but the answer is 
JSON, for tools rather than people: the web client gets it as a data 
packet, telnet as plain text. Not every part answers in JSON yet: 
functions still answer as text.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>jstat world
jstat papi affects
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>